# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=..., set by the tsan test preset). Every entry needs a
# justification. Prefer fixing the code; TSan runs nightly and is advisory (docs/testing.md).
#
# libarrow and libparquet (conda-forge) are not built with TSan: the synchronization inside Arrow's thread pools and
# futures (e.g. the I/O pool that pre-buffers Parquet column chunks) is invisible to TSan, so a buffer that an Arrow
# I/O thread frees after the reader is done is reported as racing with the reader's earlier memcpy (first seen in the
# nightly of 2026-09-26: BaseMemoryPoolImpl<SystemAllocator>::Free vs snappy decompression). Suppress race reports
# whose stacks run through these libraries. Deliberately `race:` and not `called_from_lib:`: ignoring the libraries'
# interceptors hides their mutex locks, and an unlock that Arrow's inlined future callbacks then perform in another
# library is reported as "unlock of an unlocked mutex". Races confined to our own code are still reported.
race:libarrow.so
race:libparquet.so

# DuckDB 2.0.0 (conda-forge, test oracle). Recheck these Linux reports with pixi run tsan on
# the next DuckDB upgrade. Access stacks: https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/issues/271
# Nightly runs 45616991058, 45819101495, 45824073976 and 45830643662 and a Linux x86-64
# reproduction show the following handoffs inside the oracle.
#
# Parquet scans: a worker releases its read-ahead task as the consumer frees the job. Other
# reports pair a worker's positional file read with a Thrift buffer read or file close, growth
# of its buffer handle vector with destruction of the reader's cached handles, and BlockHandle
# construction with unpinning that block. OpenMarkedFile reads a worker-created file state, and
# the worker checks a cached file's path while the consumer disposes of the handle. The worker
# also accesses that handle during ParquetReader destruction.
race:duckdb::ReadAheadIOTask::~ReadAheadIOTask(
race:duckdb::LocalFileSystem::Read(duckdb::FileHandle&, void*, long, unsigned long)
race:_M_realloc_append<duckdb::FileBufferHandleGroup::MemoryHandle>(
race:duckdb::StandardBufferManager::Unpin(duckdb::shared_ptr<duckdb::BlockHandle, true>&)
race:duckdb::MultiFileReaderData::MultiFileReaderData(duckdb::OpenFileInfo const&)
race:std::_Sp_counted_deleter<duckdb::CachingFileHandle*, std::default_delete<duckdb::CachingFileHandle>,*>::_M_dispose()
race:duckdb::ParquetReader::~ParquetReader()

# Parquet fixture creation: row-group preparation and batch flushes race with writer and file
# initialization. A queued write reads a payload filled by the producer, and the producer
# reads a formatted string from another worker. Copies of column names race with writer construction.
# The dictionary predicate integration test reports a worker copying identifiers as DuckDB reads them.
race:duckdb::ParquetWriter::PrepareRowGroup(
race:duckdb::CopyToFileGlobalState::InitializeFileState(duckdb::PendingFileState)
race:duckdb::ManagedAsyncWriteStreamQueue::CoalescedWritePayload::Ptr()
race:duckdb::AsyncFileWriter::WriteDataInternal(unsigned char const*, unsigned long)
race:duckdb::make_uniq<duckdb::StandardColumnWriter<*, duckdb::ParquetCastOperator>, duckdb::ParquetWriter&,
race:duckdb::make_uniq<duckdb::StandardColumnWriter<duckdb::string_t, duckdb::string_t, duckdb::ParquetStringOperator>,
race:duckdb::make_uniq<duckdb::StructColumnWriter,
race:duckdb::ColumnWriter::ColumnWriter(duckdb::ParquetWriter&,
race:duckdb::IdentifiersToStrings[abi:cxx11](

# DuckDB's bundled jemalloc initializes a decay mutex while another thread acquires it,
# and reads arena statistics while a worker maps or initializes the arena.
race:^duckdb_je_decay_init$
race:^duckdb_je_arena_stats_merge$
